  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1219 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nPresent model agreement continues to see the upper-level trough\npushes further east over the weekend, with most runs placing it in\nthe Northern Great Plains by Saturday. This placement will look to\nbenefit the Panhandles as it will force yet another weak cold\nfront down into the area late that day with potential to linger\ninto early Sunday morning. This cold front as well as any linger\nboundaries will provide us with decent lifting mechanisms\nresulting in better chances of widespread showers and\nthunderstorms for both days. As it stands present ensembles do\nlike our chances with some areas showing around 40 to 60 percent\nchance of seeing precipitation. Of course, a lot of this will ride\non the cold front timing and positioning, which still has a lot of\nuncertainty in the present model runs. Regardless, present\nagreement has been favoring a more active outlook for next week\nwith models suggesting a series of upper-level trough pushing in\nfrom the West Coast. Otherwise, look for cooler temperatures to\nfollow this more active pattern with afternoon highs getting into\nthe low to upper 80s as early as Sunday with chances to see upper\n70s by Tuesday.",
